Gary speaks on the 10th,

00:02:58.350 --> 00:03:00.894
so if you're gonna come, come the 10th.

00:03:00.894 --> 00:03:02.940
So a little about myself,

00:03:02.940 --> 00:03:04.510
traditional start up guy,

00:03:04.510 --> 00:03:06.494
had raised money before with companies,

00:03:06.494 --> 00:03:08.970
had made every effort to
get in front of this guy,

00:03:08.970 --> 00:03:10.250
would come to these types of events,

00:03:10.250 --> 00:03:13.410
try to rub shoulders
with him when he'd speak

00:03:13.410 --> 00:03:15.660
and now on stage with
him which is amazing.

00:03:15.660 --> 00:03:18.190
So about two years ago,

00:03:18.190 --> 00:03:19.930
started with just Shaun,

00:03:19.930 --> 00:03:22.800
I literally didn't know
people made money on YouTube.

00:03:22.800 --> 00:03:24.160
- He didn't know who PewDiePie was

00:03:24.160 --> 00:03:24.993
when he came to work for me.

00:03:24.993 --> 00:03:26.120
I'm like, alright, let's dig into YouTube.

00:03:26.120 --> 00:03:27.955
So you know PewDiePie and
he's like, "Wait who?"

00:03:27.955 --> 00:03:30.132
I was like, "Alright, we've
got a lot of work to do."

00:03:30.132 --> 00:03:31.260
- I didn't know who Casey was,

00:03:31.260 --> 00:03:33.330
really, really oblivious to the scene.

00:03:33.330 --> 00:03:36.160
Came on with Shaun from
a business perspective,

00:03:36.160 --> 00:03:37.730
not as much like oh, I want to get famous,

00:03:37.730 --> 00:03:39.120
I want to get numbers

00:03:39.120 --> 00:03:41.260
and from that business
perspective I had one goal

00:03:41.260 --> 00:03:43.040
which was make money and scale.

00:03:43.040 --> 00:03:44.500
So we jumped in with Shaun,

00:03:44.500 --> 00:03:47.020
started making money and
scaling which was amazing

00:03:47.020 --> 00:03:48.220
and then from there,

00:03:48.220 --> 00:03:52.057
found that there was so
much overflow off of Shaun.

00:03:52.057 --> 00:03:53.530
And so we started picking up,

00:03:53.530 --> 00:03:55.400
one of those overflows was from Gary.

00:03:55.400 --> 00:03:57.011
So Gary would kick some stuff,

00:03:57.011 --> 00:03:59.780
kind of unique opportunities
and invitations

00:03:59.780 --> 00:04:01.660
and kind of connections

00:04:01.660 --> 00:04:03.930
and then we took and started saying,

00:04:03.930 --> 00:04:06.750
wait, what if we worked
with other influencers?

00:04:06.750 --> 00:04:08.290
And so we started working
with other influencers

00:04:08.290 --> 00:04:10.030
and from there we built
a talent management

00:04:10.030 --> 00:04:12.050
called Spacestation Integrations.

00:04:12.050 --> 00:04:14.716
Now we work with some of the
biggest talent on YouTube.

00:04:14.716 --> 00:04:19.300
- Shaun, talk to me
about the jewelry company

00:04:19.300 --> 00:04:20.710
after you read Crush It?

00:04:20.710 --> 00:04:22.271
- Oh, I was gonna keep that one a secret.

00:04:22.271 --> 00:04:24.895
- Bring it, bring it because
I think it's super important

00:04:24.895 --> 00:04:26.460
because I think for a lot
of people that are watching

00:04:26.460 --> 00:04:28.606
and for even a bunch of us in this room,

00:04:28.606 --> 00:04:31.630
I started off as a wine retailer.

00:04:31.630 --> 00:04:34.449
I think the thing that
most people struggle,

00:04:34.449 --> 00:04:35.290
and when I look around this room,

00:04:35.290 --> 00:04:38.360
all of us have one to
three more chapters in us,

00:04:38.360 --> 00:04:40.360
I think people struggle with understanding

00:04:40.360 --> 00:04:44.830
how deep the innovation and disruption

00:04:44.830 --> 00:04:46.840
that the internet is actually causing.

00:04:46.840 --> 00:04:49.230
I think that a lot of
people see the final result

00:04:49.230 --> 00:04:51.800
but they don't understand
the steps that take there.

00:04:51.800 --> 00:04:53.820
So off of reading Crush It,

00:04:53.820 --> 00:04:54.653
what were you doing

00:04:54.653 --> 00:04:55.810
and then what did you do next?

00:04:55.810 --> 00:04:57.530
- So I was in college

00:04:57.530 --> 00:04:58.940
'cause I didn't know what
I wanted to do with my life

00:04:58.940 --> 00:05:00.680
but I wanted to do something really cool

00:05:00.680 --> 00:05:02.470
and my teacher had me read Crush It

00:05:02.470 --> 00:05:05.180
by this guy named Gary Vee or something

00:05:05.180 --> 00:05:06.330
so I'm like, alright,
let's read this thing.

00:05:06.330 --> 00:05:08.710
Read it, I was like, oh
dang, this is incredible,

00:05:08.710 --> 00:05:10.090
I need to figure this stuff out.

00:05:10.090 --> 00:05:12.031
So I started running my own business,

00:05:12.031 --> 00:05:13.160
which was a skateboard/snowboard shop.

00:05:13.160 --> 00:05:15.130
Coolest part about owning a
skateboard/snowboard shop,

00:05:15.130 --> 00:05:16.120
you literally just chill

00:05:16.120 --> 00:05:18.310
and watch snowboard
videos all day, it's dope.

00:05:18.310 --> 00:05:20.030
Worst part about owning a snowboard shop,

00:05:20.030 --> 00:05:21.690
you literally just chill
and watch videos all day,

00:05:21.690 --> 00:05:23.610
you don't sell anything, it's not dope.

00:05:23.610 --> 00:05:25.930
So Crush It helped me realize,

00:05:25.930 --> 00:05:27.060
there's so much more out there,

00:05:27.060 --> 00:05:28.740
there's different platforms

00:05:28.740 --> 00:05:29.810
where you can share a message,

00:05:29.810 --> 00:05:30.643
sell a product,

00:05:30.643 --> 00:05:31.690
give a service, whatever

00:05:31.690 --> 00:05:33.580
and that's when I wanted
to try something new.

00:05:33.580 --> 00:05:35.520
So I wanted to figure out the internet.

00:05:35.520 --> 00:05:36.890
Internet was killing my sales

00:05:36.890 --> 00:05:38.630
'cause everyone bought their stuff online,

00:05:38.630 --> 00:05:39.740
free returns, everything else.

00:05:39.740 --> 00:05:41.310
So I wanted to figure out

00:05:41.310 --> 00:05:43.380
how can I sell skateboards,
snowboards online.

00:05:43.380 --> 00:05:44.240
After reading Crush It, I was like,

00:05:44.240 --> 00:05:45.340
wait, this isn't the best idea.

00:05:45.340 --> 00:05:46.690
This is working harder,

00:05:46.690 --> 00:05:47.590
not necessarily smarter.

00:05:47.590 --> 00:05:48.430
I love snowboards

00:05:48.430 --> 00:05:50.190
but it doesn't mean I need to sell them.

00:05:50.190 --> 00:05:51.550
So I really put together a business plan

00:05:51.550 --> 00:05:53.170
of what would be the most effective way

00:05:53.170 --> 00:05:54.939
to start my first online business.

00:05:54.939 --> 00:05:57.615
And I came to the conclusion of jewelry.

00:05:57.615 --> 00:05:59.340
It was small, it was lightweight,

00:05:59.340 --> 00:06:01.010
there was a huge market for it

00:06:01.010 --> 00:06:02.260
and the platform I chose

00:06:02.260 --> 00:06:04.550
to build my business on
was Facebook at the time

00:06:04.550 --> 00:06:06.490
kind of the very first
social media platform

00:06:06.490 --> 00:06:07.980
that really hit hard.

00:06:07.980 --> 00:06:12.558
I ran the entire jewelry
boutique under my wife's name

00:06:12.558 --> 00:06:13.391
'cause I thought it was a little creepy

00:06:13.391 --> 00:06:15.210
like skater kid running a jewelry boutique

00:06:15.210 --> 00:06:16.060
out of the back of his shop.

00:06:16.060 --> 00:06:18.640
So it was all under her name, rainy day,

00:06:18.640 --> 00:06:20.760
alright, ladies, what movie
are you gonna watch today?

00:06:20.760 --> 00:06:21.770
And they'd be like, The Notebook

00:06:21.770 --> 00:06:23.124
and I'd be like, already seen it.

00:06:23.124 --> 00:06:24.950
It got weird, guys,

00:06:24.950 --> 00:06:27.600
but it taught me a lot
about building a business

00:06:27.600 --> 00:06:29.402
and the power of social media.

00:06:29.402 --> 00:06:30.625
So from there,

00:06:30.625 --> 00:06:32.840
I was like, oh, this is the real deal,

00:06:32.840 --> 00:06:33.990
scaled that in one year,

00:06:33.990 --> 00:06:34.900
was able to sell it,

00:06:34.900 --> 00:06:36.400
had actual money in my pockets,

00:06:36.400 --> 00:06:37.410
paid off student loans

00:06:37.410 --> 00:06:39.750
and started what would
be my next business,

00:06:39.750 --> 00:06:41.090
which was in social media

00:06:41.090 --> 00:06:42.257
and that's where I identified Snapchat

00:06:42.257 --> 00:06:43.410
and took it from there.

00:06:43.410 --> 00:06:46.190
So from reading Gary's book Crush It

00:06:46.190 --> 00:06:47.920
to executing on that,

00:06:47.920 --> 00:06:49.350
finding success,

00:06:49.350 --> 00:06:50.268
digging deeper

00:06:50.268 --> 00:06:52.320
and then I was just bragging,

00:06:52.320 --> 00:06:54.280
I'm the very first quote in Crushing It.

00:06:54.280 --> 00:06:56.573
So only one person has the
first quote in Crushing It,

00:06:56.573 --> 00:06:57.530
it's me.

00:06:57.530 --> 00:06:59.030
- Limited real estate, Shaun.

00:06:59.030 --> 00:07:02.697
So Holladay, how did you get to Shaun?

00:07:02.697 --> 00:07:04.190
So you're a start up kid,

00:07:04.190 --> 00:07:06.040
you're playing in that world,

00:07:06.040 --> 00:07:08.050
how'd you find Shaun,

00:07:08.050 --> 00:07:08.883
what played out?

00:07:08.883 --> 00:07:09.716
- Yeah, so little background,

00:07:09.716 --> 00:07:11.600
Shaun and I, Shonduras the name

00:07:11.600 --> 00:07:14.920
was from a mission that
we went to in Honduras.

00:07:14.920 --> 00:07:15.753
So when he got home,

00:07:15.753 --> 00:07:17.622
they called him Shaun
from Honduras, Shonduras.

00:07:17.622 --> 00:07:19.370
So that's kind of the history of the name.

00:07:19.370 --> 00:07:21.560
So we knew each other
there just a little bit,

00:07:21.560 --> 00:07:22.910
nothing crazy though.

00:07:22.910 --> 00:07:23.743
When I got back,

00:07:23.743 --> 00:07:25.180
I was running my start up,

00:07:25.180 --> 00:07:26.750
and was super deep

00:07:26.750 --> 00:07:28.803
and Shaun was coming into
town for a brand deal

00:07:28.803 --> 00:07:31.240
and naysayers like, hey,
can I stay with you?

00:07:31.240 --> 00:07:32.140
I don't want to stay at this hotel.

00:07:32.140 --> 00:07:32.990
I was like, sure.

00:07:32.990 --> 00:07:34.540
So he slept on the floor at my house.

00:07:34.540 --> 00:07:35.810
- Whoa, whoa, we didn't sleep,

00:07:35.810 --> 00:07:37.400
we stayed up all night talking.

00:07:37.400 --> 00:07:38.300
- After we stayed up till four.

00:07:38.300 --> 00:07:40.420
- The plan was to sleep on the floor.

00:07:40.420 --> 00:07:41.633
- Is that how you rolled back then,

00:07:41.633 --> 00:07:43.240
you wouldn't want to go
to hotels, you just like?

00:07:43.240 --> 00:07:45.180
- Oh yeah, everything is networking,

00:07:45.180 --> 00:07:46.940
connections, old friends.
I saw he was killing it.

00:07:46.940 --> 00:07:48.700
He had his own start up
business that crushed it

00:07:48.700 --> 00:07:50.730
and I was like, dude, I
want to learn from you.

00:07:50.730 --> 00:07:51.610
I'm doing the Snapchat thing,

00:07:51.610 --> 00:07:52.520
you did your thing,

00:07:52.520 --> 00:07:53.810
let's hang out and jam.

00:07:53.810 --> 00:07:55.823
Spent the whole night talking,
next thing you know I'm like,

00:07:55.823 --> 00:07:58.030
dude, I'm getting way
deep into public speaking,

00:07:58.030 --> 00:08:00.110
I was kind of trying to be
Gary's understudy at the time

00:08:00.110 --> 00:08:01.360
and if Gary didn't do a deal,

00:08:01.360 --> 00:08:02.193
I would do a deal.

00:08:02.193 --> 00:08:03.734
We spoke at a couple of events together

00:08:03.734 --> 00:08:05.901
and I was like, dude, I want
to crush public speaking.

00:08:05.901 --> 00:08:07.324
His previous business

00:08:07.324 --> 00:08:09.920
was an app that turned your
phone into a microphone.

00:08:09.920 --> 00:08:11.620
So anyone out there just
pulls out there phone

00:08:11.620 --> 00:08:12.776
and asks a question, super simple.

00:08:12.776 --> 00:08:16.380
I was like, you know the
speaking world, help me do this.

00:08:16.380 --> 00:08:17.213
And he helped me do it.

00:08:17.213 --> 00:08:18.420
He helped me get my first speaking gig,

00:08:18.420 --> 00:08:19.730
got me a TED Talk,

00:08:19.730 --> 00:08:21.510
provided all this value, no payment

00:08:21.510 --> 00:08:23.060
and I was like, dude, this guy hustles,

00:08:23.060 --> 00:08:24.070
how do I get him on my team?

00:08:24.070 --> 00:08:25.610
So I was like, yo, what would it take you

00:08:25.610 --> 00:08:27.930
to move you out, you and
your family out to Utah--

00:08:27.930 --> 00:08:29.500
- Real quick for everybody watching

00:08:29.500 --> 00:08:31.090
and listening on the podcast,

00:08:31.090 --> 00:08:32.565
before we started this episode,

00:08:32.565 --> 00:08:35.040
with the group of 17,
25 people that are here,

00:08:35.040 --> 00:08:36.177
I said, "Look, before you leave,

00:08:36.177 --> 00:08:37.250
"make sure you say hello,"

00:08:37.250 --> 00:08:38.560
'cause I've been watching
them for the last hour

00:08:38.560 --> 00:08:41.210
and a lot of people haven't
said hello to each other.

00:08:43.081 --> 00:08:44.330
I love when you,

00:08:44.330 --> 00:08:46.283
Instagram is a limiting platform for me

00:08:46.283 --> 00:08:49.190
which is why the most
motivational version of myself

00:08:49.190 --> 00:08:50.023
is on that platform.

00:08:50.023 --> 00:08:52.170
With one minute video being the length

00:08:52.170 --> 00:08:53.560
and pictures and quotes,

00:08:53.560 --> 00:08:55.490
there's only one part of
what I can show there.

00:08:55.490 --> 00:08:57.440
But there's a quote
that I put on Instagram,

00:08:57.440 --> 00:08:59.925
it just says, people are the ROI.

00:08:59.925 --> 00:09:03.410
And you can only do so
much to explain a post

